# Local development only.
#
# In production NOTHING here is needed. The Apps Script url and the shared
# token live in Vercel's own environment variables, read at request time by
# api/submit.ts, and never reach the browser. Anything named VITE_* is
# substituted into the bundle at build time and is therefore public.
#
# Set these in Vercel > Project > Settings > Environment Variables:
#
#   SHEETS_ENDPOINT   https://script.google.com/macros/s/XXXXXXXX/exec
#   SUBMIT_TOKEN      must match SUBMIT_TOKEN in server/Code.gs
#
# Note the lack of a VITE_ prefix. That is the whole point.

# `vite dev` has no /api behind it, so submissions are logged to the console
# instead. Uncomment to post for real -- either at `vercel dev`, which does
# serve the function, or straight at Apps Script.
# VITE_SUBMIT_URL=/api/submit
